# Dagric OS Pro — Developer toolchain
# "Zero-friction setup out of the box."

# Containers
#
# docker-cli IS THE `docker` COMMAND AND IT IS NOT OPTIONAL. In Debian 13 the
# client was split out of docker.io, which now ships only /usr/sbin/dockerd,
# /usr/sbin/docker-proxy and /usr/bin/docker-init — verified against Debian's
# own file list for trixie/amd64/docker.io. docker-cli is a RECOMMENDS, and
# --apt-recommends false is in force for this whole build, so it was dropped:
# out/manifest/pro.packages has docker.io and no docker-cli.
#
# The result shipped on the 3.9 GB Pro ISO. A buyer opens Konsole, types the
# first line of every Docker tutorial — `docker run hello-world` — and gets
# "docker: command not found", with the daemon running fine underneath. The Pro
# page sells "Docker + Compose, Podman, Distrobox ... all preinstalled". That is
# a refund conversation caused by a Recommends nobody could see.
#
# passt provides pasta, the default rootless network backend for podman 5, and
# is likewise only a Recommends. Without it `podman run` as a normal user fails
# to set up networking — and site/pro.html promises "Podman runs rootless the
# moment you open a terminal", offered as the safe alternative to adding
# yourself to the docker group. slirp0netns is the older fallback and is listed
# too so an owner following any tutorial written before netavark finds it there.
docker.io
docker-cli
docker-compose
podman
passt
slirp4netns

# Any distro in a terminal: run Ubuntu/Fedora/Arch toolchains inside
# containers with full host integration (audio, GPU, home dir) —
# legacy tools without polluting the host
distrobox

# Core toolchain
build-essential
git
python3-pip
python3-venv

# SSH — client for reaching servers, server present but DISABLED by
# default (enable with: sudo systemctl enable --now ssh)
openssh-client
openssh-server

# Modern terminal quality-of-life: readable apt front-end with history/undo,
# syntax-highlighted cat, and a cd that learns your directories
nala
bat
zoxide
